{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787270009170759001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"undamaged-epidermic-kakarikis","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"503b7d3452e560c5c6ac006c2e95aad4a1132403223de3b6dae32b32bc602c46","event_uuid":"5cfacffd-3ed2-4e22-8a03-5dfe53ebe00f","position":{"commit_sha":"74e186af431bf3d1384089d2a064caccf2178344","position":"1787266164422457001-5cfacffd-3ed2-4e22-8a03-5dfe53ebe00f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2c7eabbb114b0ff72bd040671ff99beaca4636a2c8bc03125db999c4d7b441bd","event_uuid":"33e7513d-66e0-4c1a-82e3-8b078ebb8c96","position":{"commit_sha":"4482a29ffac730f0c1d10de0da68bd8db0c6af71","position":"1787266176004830001-33e7513d-66e0-4c1a-82e3-8b078ebb8c96"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787266164422457001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"33e7513d-66e0-4c1a-82e3-8b078ebb8c96","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3907-0110-7688-43bd"}],"description":"## Discovered from\n\nrebar-debug on bug `itchy-arbored-peccary` (3907-0110-7688-43bd), while verifying a handed-in\nclaim that the janitor had no caller. It has one — but exactly one.\n\n## Problem\n\n`start_background_janitor` has a single production invocation: the review-bot's FastAPI\nlifespan, `src/rebar/review_bot/app.py:134-136` (documented at\n`infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md:500-501`). Confirmed by both a plain `grep` for the name as a\nstring and a semantic `find_referencing_symbols`; the two agree.\n\nSo the janitor — the ONLY thing that reclaims `$REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR/rebar-gate-snapshots` — runs\nonly inside the long-lived review-bot server process. Every other host that resolves an attested\ngate runs no janitor at all:\n\n- a developer laptop running `rebar review-plan` / `review-code` / `verify-completion`\n- a CI runner invoking the same gates\n- any embedding of the library that is not the review-bot FastAPI app\n\nOn those hosts the store is append-only for the life of the machine. Measured on one developer\nhost (read-only inspection, nothing deleted):\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| entries in the store | 64,021 |\n| of which `tickets-<sha>` | 34,851 |\n| size of a recent `tickets-<sha>` | ~861 MiB |\n| `bytes.total` reports | 47.24 GiB |\n\nNothing has ever reclaimed any of it.\n\n## Why this is separate from 3907\n\n3907 fixes the *policy*: it implements the ADR-promised byte-total cap and makes the tickets\nentries byte-accounted, so a size trigger exists and reads a true total. That is necessary but\nit only helps where a janitor pass actually runs. This ticket is about the *cadence* — there is\nno pass to apply the policy on any non-review-bot host.\n\n## Constraint\n\nADR 0005 D5 is explicit that the janitor is \"off the hot path ... never invoked from\npopulate/read\", so a naive GC call inside `cache.acquire` would contradict the recorded\narchitecture and put an `flock` + full `iterdir` on every gate resolution. A design is needed,\nnot a one-liner. Sketches worth evaluating:\n\n- an **operation-linked opportunistic pass** that is off the *critical* path — e.g. after a gate\n  RESOLVES (not during populate), rate-limited by a stamp file so at most one pass runs per\n  `interval_seconds` per host, and skipped entirely if the gc `flock` is contended\n- a `rebar snapshot-gc` **CLI verb** an operator or a CI step can call explicitly, plus\n  documentation of it in `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md`\n- starting the background thread from any long-lived rebar process, not just the review-bot app\n\nThe portability criterion (`project.portability`) rules out a fix whose only trigger is a\nspecific CI system; an operation-linked or in-process trigger is required.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A host that runs attested gates WITHOUT the review-bot server reclaims its snapshot store.\n- [ ] The chosen trigger does not put GC work on the populate/read hot path (ADR 0005 D5 holds,\n      or the ADR is amended with the reasoning).\n- [ ] The trigger is operation-linked or in-process — not dependent on any one CI provider.\n- [ ] A test observes reclamation happening on a simulated non-review-bot host RED before /\n      GREEN after.\n- [ ] `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md` documents when a pass runs and how an operator forces one.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"58a3-0756-e470-4b40","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Snapshot janitor runs only in the review-bot process; every other host's store is append-only","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5cfacffd-3ed2-4e22-8a03-5dfe53ebe00f","33e7513d-66e0-4c1a-82e3-8b078ebb8c96"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787270009170759001,"uuid":"d9569a93-9a19-4f7b-acd1-17c21e9c6782"}